From 77d343b7990c5d572ab2a4bc51b5749ae2f1ff17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hiper25 <whydonit@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:34:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: staging: meson: vdec: do not abort session on
 broadcast H.264 frame_num gap

In live DVB/PVR broadcast streams, packet drops and non-reference frame
discontinuities frequently produce frame_num gaps when frame_num_gap_allowed
is zero in the active SPS. Previously, the driver treated this as a fatal
decoding error (-EILSEQ) and invoked amvdec_abort(), permanently stopping
video frame delivery and leaving the display in a black screen state.

Do not abort the session on frame_num gaps; allow decoding to continue
so that recovery can occur at the next reference or IDR picture.

Signed-off-by: Linux Amlogic SC2 Maintainer <maintainers@libreelec.tv>
---
 drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_h264.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_h264.c b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_h264.c
index 732be92eeb9f..6b48425dbb95 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_h264.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_h264.c
@@ -5025,7 +5025,6 @@ static irqreturn_t h264_multi_threaded_isr(struct amvdec_session *sess)
         }
         ret = meson_h264_dpb_h264_slice_header_process(dpb, &gap);
         if (ret < 0 || dpb->dpb_error_flag ||
-            (gap && !dpb->mSPS.frame_num_gap_allowed) ||
             dpb->mSlice.slice_type >= NUM_SLICE_TYPES) {
             dev_err(core->dev, "H264 MULTI DPB failed: ret=%d error=%d gap=%d allowed=%d type=%d\n",
                     ret, dpb->dpb_error_flag, gap,
-- 
2.47.3

